cix-panda-vision-grasp
======================

This repository is a fork of laoxue888/Moveit2YoloObb
(https://github.com/laoxue888/Moveit2YoloObb, MIT License, Copyright (c) 2025
DimensionalEngineer). The upstream MIT License is retained in LICENSE and
applies to all files inherited from upstream.

Upstream base: commit ce16f5a (2026-03-18), the tip of the upstream repository
at the time of the fork.

CIX Technology Group modifications (Copyright 2026 Cix Technology Group Co.,
Ltd, Apache-2.0) include:

- CIX P1 (CD8180, aarch64) board adaptation: ARM64 build fixes, Mali GPU /
  ZINK long-run guidance, localhost-only DDS configuration.
- NPU YOLO inference backend: runs detection on the CIX NPU via the
  `cix_ros_noe_yolo` package from the CIX Robotics SDK (not vendored here),
  alongside the original Ultralytics backend.
- `start_all.sh` orchestration (deps / build / start / stop), stale-process
  cleanup, and per-component logging.
- Adaptation and startup documentation (docs/).

Files carrying CIX copyright headers are CIX modifications; everything else
is inherited from upstream.

Robot assets
------------

`ros2_project/src/robot_description` is the `panda_description` package from
moveit_resources (https://github.com/moveit-resources/panda_description,
BSD-3-Clause). Its Panda arm meshes are derived from `franka_description`
(https://github.com/frankaemika/franka_description, Apache-2.0, Copyright
Franka Robotics GmbH).

`GraphExecuter/` is vendored from the upstream repository's submodule of the
same name and carries its own LICENSE.

The Gazebo world models under
`ros2_project/src/panda_moveit_config/worlds/` (hammer, monkey_wrench,
ground_plane, sun, table) are derived from the OSRF `gazebo_models`
repository (https://github.com/osrf/gazebo_models, Apache-2.0, Copyright
Open Source Robotics Foundation).

The `cole_hammer` world model is derived from the Google Scanned Objects
dataset (Copyright 2020 Google LLC, CC BY 4.0); its mesh files retain the
CC BY 4.0 attribution.

Weights files
-------------

The CPU-backend YOLO OBB weights file `best.pt` is NOT distributed with this
repository (Ultralytics YOLOv8 weights are licensed AGPL-3.0,
https://docs.ultralytics.com/models/yolov8/). Users download the copy trained
by the upstream author from the upstream repository (see README).

The NPU-backend compiled model `ros2_project/models/yolo_obb.cix` IS
distributed with this repository. It is compiled from the same Ultralytics
YOLOv8 OBB checkpoint and is therefore also licensed AGPL-3.0, applying to
that file on top of the repository's MIT / Apache-2.0 code licensing.
`start_all.sh` passes it to `cix_ros_noe_yolo` via `npu_model_path`.
